From: mocha port <local>
Subject: [PATCH 0004] libprocessgroup/rootdir: adapt cgroup profiles to the 3.10 kernel

The A12 defaults assume cgroup v1 with cpuset+blkio+schedtune and a cgroup v2
unified hierarchy for the freezer. The Xiaomi Mi Pad 1 kernel (3.10, Tegra)
compiles CONFIG_CGROUPS/CGROUP_SCHED/CGROUP_FREEZER/MEMCG/CGROUP_CPUACCT only:
CONFIG_CPUSETS, CONFIG_BLK_CGROUP and CONFIG_SCHEDTUNE are absent and there is
no cgroup2 mount (/sys/fs/cgroup is plain sysfs).

Consequences measured in the F6 boot log (logs_f6/logcat_boot4.log):
  - "Failed to mount blkio cgroup: No such file or directory"
  - "Failed to mount cpuset cgroup: No such device" (init also asks for kmod
    fs-cpuset, which does not exist)
  - 574 x "Failed to add task into cgroup" (JoinCgroup actions for cpuset/blkio)
  - "Controller freezer is not found" + "SetAttribute: unknown attribute:
    FreezerState" (no cgroup2 freezer)
  - init.rc cpuset copy/mkdir failures and
    "property 'ro.bionic.2nd_arch' doesn't exist" (arm32-only device)

Keep every profile name (Java callers resolve them) but drop the actions that
reference controllers this kernel cannot provide, drop the cpu.uclamp.*
attributes (utilclamp arrived in 5.3) and the unsupported SetClamps actions,
and remove the init.rc blocks that only produced errors.
